# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for the rendered chart.
#
# The CI gate is `--severity HIGH,CRITICAL`, and the default render currently
# has none, so this file holds no suppressions. It is not empty of purpose: the
# LOW/MEDIUM findings below are deliberate, and anyone lowering the threshold
# should read this before silencing them.
#
#   KSV-0011  CPU not limited. Deliberate. The adapter's work is a poll loop
#             against Clair; throttling it delays reports without making
#             anything safer. Set resources.limits.cpu if your platform
#             requires one.
#   KSV-0020  Runs with UID <= 10000. The adapter runs as exactly 10000, which
#             is what the image's /home/scanner tree is owned by.
#   KSV-0021  Runs with GID <= 10000. Same reason.
#   KSV-0110  Workloads in the default namespace. An artifact of scanning a
#             `helm template` render with no --namespace, not of the chart.
#   KSV-0125  Restrict container images to trusted registries. The default
#             registry is ours; air-gapped users repoint it with
#             global.imageRegistry.
